<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Cash basis steady to higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Cash basis steady to higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash soymeal basis values were steady to higher Friday largely in reaction to news soybean processors decreased production this week, dealers said.</p>
<p>Also, a few dealers said there was slight increase in demand early Friday in reaction to the lower crush. They said buyers bought supplies ahead of anticipated price increases related to the reduced supply.</p>
<p>The National Oilseed Processors Association reported late Thursday the crush for the week ended March 19 at 28.121 million bushels, versus 30.106 million the previous week.</p>
<p>The crush also was less than what many soymeal dealers had expected.  </p>
